-- 370 Deakin -> Deakin RTP / DUPRS (AUD 37,450 p.a.)
UPDATE scholarships SET
  title = 'Deakin Research Training Program (RTP) and Postgraduate Research Scholarship (DUPRS)',
  provider = 'Deakin University',
  coverage_type = 'Full Tuition + Stipend',
  amount_usd_value = 0,
  deadline = $dl$Round-based. The international round for the February 2027 intake opened 6 July 2026 and closed 23 August 2026 (outcomes by 6 November 2026). Dates for the next international round are not yet published on Deakin's scholarship page; domestic rounds run on their own dates and are not the route for students from Uzbekistan.$dl$,
  degree_levels = $json$["Master's","PhD"]$json$,
  eligible_majors = $json$["All research fields in which Deakin enrols graduate research candidates"]$json$,
  eligible_countries = $json$["All countries"]$json$,
  min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL,
  financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true,
  description = $desc$Deakin University awards its main research-degree scholarships under two names on one competitive application: the Australian Government Research Training Program Scholarship (RTP) and the Deakin University Postgraduate Research Scholarship (DUPRS), funded by Deakin itself. Both are open to domestic and international candidates, and Deakin notes only top-ranked applicants are offered an RTP. The package pays a living stipend of AUD 37,450 per annum, tax exempt, a relocation allowance of AUD 500 to AUD 1,500 (single to family) for candidates moving interstate or overseas to study at Deakin, a tuition fees offset, and, for international candidates only, a single Overseas Student Health Cover (OSHC) policy for the duration of the student visa. Duration is three years of stipend and four years of tuition fees offset for a doctorate, and two years of each for a research masters. Holders are enrolled as on-campus full-time candidates.$desc$,
  requirements = $req$Be a domestic or international student enrolled (or applying to enrol) in a graduate research course at Deakin University. For a stipend, Deakin requires at least four years of tertiary study, a result of 80% or equivalent in the research component of previous study (or equivalent attainment considering previous study, relevant work experience, publications and other research experience), and all minimum entry requirements under Deakin's HDR Admission, Selection and Enrolment Procedure. Recipients of an RTP Fees Offset must not be receiving an equivalent Commonwealth award designed to offset graduate research fees. Prospective candidates apply through Deakin's research degree application process by the closing date of the relevant round; currently enrolled graduate researchers use a separate form and cannot apply after completing more than three years of a doctorate or two years of a masters.$req$,
  funding_type = 'Australian Government Research Training Program (RTP) and university-funded DUPRS: living stipend, tuition fees offset, relocation allowance, and single OSHC for international candidates',
  tuition_coverage = 'A tuition fees offset is part of the award: four years for a doctorate and two years for a research masters (the stipend runs three and two years respectively), so international tuition is offset for that period rather than billed.',
  living_allowance = 37450,
  english_requirements = 'English language minima sit in Deakin''s research degree entry requirements and HDR admission procedure linked from the scholarship page; no single English score is published on the scholarship page itself, so none is stored here.',
  required_documents = $json$["Research degree application to Deakin University by the round closing date (scholarship consideration runs with admission)","Academic transcripts showing at least four years of tertiary study and the research component result","Evidence of research experience and outputs (publications, thesis/research component details)","English proficiency evidence per Deakin HDR entry requirements"]$json$,
  website_url = 'https://www.deakin.edu.au/study/fees-and-scholarships/scholarships/find-a-scholarship/rtp-and-duprs',
  source_url = 'https://www.deakin.edu.au/study/fees-and-scholarships/scholarships/find-a-scholarship/rtp-and-duprs',
  application_url = 'https://www.deakin.edu.au/research/research-degrees/how-to-apply-for-a-research-degree',
  deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL,
  rounds = $json$[{"round":"2027 international round (February 2027 intake)","opens":"2026-07-06","closes":"2026-08-23","outcome_by":"2026-11-06"},{"round":"2027 domestic round (February 2027 intake, Australian/NZ applicants)","opens":"2026-07-06","closes":"2026-10-25","outcome_by":"2026-12-23"}]$json$,
  recurrence = 'annual',
  expected_opening_period = NULL,
  expected_deadline_period = $exp$Deakin runs named rounds: the 2027 international round (February 2027 intake) opened 6 July 2026 and closed 23 August 2026. Dates for the next international round had not been published when the page was read on 2026-10-26; expect a similar mid-year window and verify on Deakin's page.$exp$,
  application_status = 'closed',
  verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true,
  last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(),
  notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (pass 97) from Deakin's official 'Research Training Program Scholarship (RTP) / Deakin University Postgraduate Research Scholarship (DUPR)' page fetched the same day: stipend AUD 37,450 p.a. tax exempt; relocation allowance AUD 500-1,500; single OSHC for international candidates for the visa duration; doctoral tenure 3 years stipend / 4 years fees offset, research masters 2/2; selection requires at least four years of tertiary study and 80% or equivalent in the research component; 2027 international round 6 July-23 August 2026 for February 2027 intake, outcomes by 6 November 2026. This replaces the earlier generic RTP-framework record (reliability 4), which had already stripped the importer's invented USD 40,000 figure and copied August 31 deadline; the AUD 37,450 figure matches the Deakin 2026 RTP/DUPR terms-and-conditions documents linked from the same page. Next international round dates are not published, so deadline_date stays NULL with deadline_type 'not_published' and the status is closed rather than a guessed 2027 date. min_gpa is NULL because Deakin expresses its bar as 80% in the research component, not a GPA; min_ielts NULL (no score on the award page). university_id set to the Deakin university record (232) and a matching university_scholarships row created in this pass; source 2510 repointed from the bare domain to the award page.$note$,
  university_id = 232,
  award_amount = 37450, award_currency = 'AUD', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'fixed'
WHERE id = 370;

-- 372 Macquarie -> International Research Scholarships (iRTP and iMQRES), AUD 40,900 p.a.
UPDATE scholarships SET
  title = 'Macquarie University International Research Scholarships (iRTP and iMQRES)',
  provider = 'Macquarie University',
  coverage_type = 'Full Tuition + Stipend',
  amount_usd_value = 0,
  deadline = $dl$The International Scholarship Round for Session 1 2027 opened 15 June 2026 and closed 31 July 2026 at 11pm (Sydney time); outcomes were released from early October 2026. Dates for the next international round are not yet published on the award page.$dl$,
  degree_levels = $json$["Master's","PhD"]$json$,
  eligible_majors = $json$["Arts and social sciences","Business","Education","Engineering","Information technologies","Language and linguistics","Law","Media, communications and creative arts","Medicine and health","Psychological sciences","Science","Security, intelligence and criminology"]$json$,
  eligible_countries = $json$["All countries except Australia and New Zealand (Australian permanent residents excluded)"]$json$,
  min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL,
  financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true,
  description = $desc$Macquarie University fills its main international research scholarships through one International Scholarship Round covering two schemes: the Australian Government International Research Training Program scholarship (iRTP) and the university-funded International Macquarie Research Excellence Scholarship (iMQRES); applicants for an iRTP are automatically considered for the iMQRES in the same round. Successful PhD applicants under either scheme receive a tuition fee offset for a maximum of three years and a living allowance stipend of AUD 40,900 per annum for up to three years; iRTP holders additionally receive a Sydney transport (Opal) travel concession. The round is for full-time Master of Research and PhD candidature based in Sydney, ranked competitively on academic merit, research output and experience, and alignment with Macquarie's research strategy. Applicants who do not yet meet PhD admission criteria may be counter-offered MRes entry with a provisional PhD place or a scholarship covering the MRes portion.$desc$,
  requirements = $req$At the time of application: be a citizen of a country other than Australia or New Zealand and not an Australian permanent resident; intend to reside in Sydney during the candidature; plan to start a full-time Master of Research or PhD in Session 1 2027; meet the admission criteria (including the English language requirement) for the Macquarie research degree; hold a valid visa for onshore study from Session 1 2027; have already completed the qualifying degree (final-semester students are generally ineligible, except Macquarie students and Macquarie Business School PhD applicants); and hold confirmation of supervision from an eligible Macquarie researcher (compulsory in most faculties). Excluded: students who started a Macquarie graduate research program before 1 July 2026, holders of another equivalent major award, applicants who already completed a research degree at the same or higher level in the same field, and incomplete applications (they are withdrawn and cannot be held over to a future round).$req$,
  funding_type = 'Australian Government iRTP and Macquarie-funded iMQRES: three-year tuition fee offset plus AUD 40,900 p.a. living stipend (iRTP adds an Opal travel concession)',
  tuition_coverage = 'Tuition fee offset for a maximum of three years for successful PhD applicants under both iRTP and iMQRES, so tuition is offset rather than billed for that period.',
  living_allowance = 40900,
  english_requirements = 'Applicants must meet Macquarie''s published English language requirement for research degrees; the scholarship page does not state a single test score, so none is stored.',
  required_documents = $json$["Graduate research application to Macquarie University selecting 'International Research Scholarship' as the scholarship type","Academic transcripts and evidence of the completed qualifying degree","Documentation of research qualifications where relevant (thesis abstract/examiner reports, publications, conference presentations)","Confirmation of supervision from an eligible Macquarie researcher (compulsory in most faculties)","English proficiency evidence meeting Macquarie's research degree requirement"]$json$,
  website_url = 'https://www.mq.edu.au/research/phd-and-research-degrees/how-to-apply/scholarship-opportunities/scholarship-search/international-scholarship-round',
  source_url = 'https://www.mq.edu.au/research/phd-and-research-degrees/how-to-apply/scholarship-opportunities/scholarship-search/international-scholarship-round',
  application_url = 'https://www.mq.edu.au/research/phd-and-research-degrees/how-to-apply/scholarship-opportunities',
  deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL,
  rounds = $json$[{"round":"International Scholarship Round, Session 1 2027 (iRTP + iMQRES)","opens":"2026-06-15","closes":"2026-07-31 23:00","outcomes":"from early October 2026 (no notification by 15 November 2026 means unsuccessful)"}]$json$,
  recurrence = 'annual',
  expected_opening_period = NULL,
  expected_deadline_period = $exp$One international round per year for Session 1 commencement: the Session 1 2027 round ran 15 June-31 July 2026. Dates for the Session 1 2028 round had not been published when the page was read on 2026-10-26.$exp$,
  application_status = 'closed',
  verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true,
  last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(),
  notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (pass 97) from Macquarie University's official International Scholarship Round page fetched the same day: one round covers the government iRTP and university iMQRES; successful PhD applicants receive a tuition fee offset (max 3 years) plus a living stipend of AUD 40,900 p.a. for up to three years, with an Opal travel concession for iRTP holders. NOTE: the page is internally inconsistent about the rate year - Key details say 'AUD 40,900 p.a. (2027 rate)' while the Components sections repeat 'at the 2026 rate' for the same AUD 40,900 figure; the figure itself is identical everywhere and is stored, and the 2027 label from Key details is followed in the text. Replaces the generic framework record (reliability 4) and the importer's 'Macquarie PhD Scholarship MQPS' name, invented USD 43,000 figure and copied August 31 deadline (already stripped in an earlier record; the stale 'USD 43000 year' string on university_scholarships row 604 was corrected in this pass). The Session 1 2027 round closed 31 July 2026 and no Session 1 2028 dates are published, so deadline_date is NULL with deadline_type 'not_published' and status closed. Min GPA/IELTS are NULL: ranking is competitive on merit, outputs and potential, and the page publishes no single cut-off. Source 2576 repointed from the bare domain to the award page.$note$,
  university_id = 119,
  award_amount = 40900, award_currency = 'AUD', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'fixed'
WHERE id = 372;

-- 373 UTS -> UTS International Research Scholarship (IRS), tuition fee (course-dependent)
UPDATE scholarships SET
  title = 'UTS International Research Scholarship (IRS)',
  provider = 'University of Technology Sydney',
  coverage_type = 'Full Tuition',
  amount_usd_value = 0,
  deadline = $dl$Applications for the current listing opened 7 September 2026 and closed 7 October 2026. UTS states applications are now closed and asks applicants to check back for future sessions; no next-round dates are published.$dl$,
  degree_levels = $json$["Master's","PhD"]$json$,
  eligible_majors = $json$["All research fields (international HDR candidates in UTS areas of research strength)"]$json$,
  eligible_countries = $json$["All countries"]$json$,
  min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL,
  financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true,
  description = $desc$The UTS International Research Scholarship (UTS IRS) is the University of Technology Sydney's tuition-fee scholarship for high-quality international students in higher degrees by research, offered as part of UTS's commitment to international research links and aimed at applicants in areas of research strength. The scholarship value is the tuition fee of the research course, for up to 3.5 years full-time for a PhD and 2 years full-time for a Master by Research. There is no separate application form for prospective students: one application covers the IRS and the associated scholarships - UTS lists its competitive research scholarships (including the Australian Government Research Training Program Stipend living allowance and the UTS President's Scholarship) as awards that applicants are considered for by indicating in their research degree application that they wish to be considered for a scholarship. The UTS base living-stipend rate is AUD 40,500 per annum tax-free commencing 1 January 2027, but that stipend is a separate associated award and is not part of the IRS itself, so this record stores tuition coverage only.$desc$,
  requirements = $req$Be an international student applying for or undertaking a Master by Research or PhD at UTS (higher degree by research), in an area of research strength, and indicate in the research degree application that you wish to be considered for UTS competitive scholarships - no separate IRS form exists for prospective students, and one application considers you for the IRS and associated awards. Awards are competitive and assessed against other applicants. UTS asks applicants to respect the scholarship application closing dates for their intended session; incomplete and late applications are not considered.$req$,
  funding_type = 'University-funded tuition fee scholarship for international HDR candidates (living stipend is a separate associated award, not part of IRS)',
  tuition_coverage = 'Covers the tuition fee of the research course (the amount depends on the course) for up to 3.5 years full-time (PhD) or 2 years full-time (Master by Research).',
  living_allowance = NULL,
  english_requirements = 'UTS research degree admission sets the English requirement per course; no single score is published on the IRS scholarship page, so none is stored.',
  required_documents = $json$["Research degree application to UTS indicating that you wish to be considered for competitive scholarships (no separate IRS application form)","Academic transcripts and research background documents required for HDR admission"]$json$,
  website_url = 'https://www.uts.edu.au/for-students/admissions-entry/scholarships/scholarships-search/international-research-scholarship',
  source_url = 'https://www.uts.edu.au/for-students/admissions-entry/scholarships/scholarships-search/international-research-scholarship',
  application_url = NULL,
  deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL,
  rounds = $json$[{"applications_open":"2026-09-07","applications_close":"2026-10-07","status":"Closed - UTS asks applicants to check back for future session announcements"}]$json$,
  recurrence = 'annual',
  expected_opening_period = NULL,
  expected_deadline_period = $exp$The most recent IRS window ran 7 September-7 October 2026 and is closed; UTS asks applicants to check back for announcements for future sessions, and research scholarship consideration is tied to the session-based research degree application closing dates.$exp$,
  application_status = 'closed',
  verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true,
  last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(),
  notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (pass 97). The importer's 'UTS Vice-Chancellor PhD Scholarship VCPS' does not correspond to a live UTS award (UTS's prestige award is the President's Scholarship), and the previous record was only the generic RTP framework at reliability 4 with the invented USD 42,000 figure already stripped. UTS's International Research Training Program Scholarship (IRTP) page returned 404 when fetched on 2026-10-26 and IRTP no longer appears in UTS's live competitive-scholarships list, so this record is written from the pages UTS currently publishes instead: the live UTS International Research Scholarship (IRS) page (tuition fee of the course covered, up to 3.5 years PhD / 2 years MRes; applications 7 September-7 October 2026, STATUS Closed; no separate application form - one form considers prospective students for IRS and associated scholarships), the live 'How to fund your PhD or Master's by Research' page (competitive scholarships are considered via the research degree application; UTS base rate AUD 40,500 from 1 January 2027) and the live Australian Government RTP Stipend page (living allowance AUD 40,500 p.a. tax-free - a separate associated award, deliberately not bundled into this record's coverage). The OSHC inclusion that appeared in the older IRTP listing is NOT claimed for IRS because the live IRS page does not mention it. award_amount is NULL (tuition fee depends on the course); amount_usd_value 0. deadline_date NULL/'not_published' (next session dates unpublished). The stale 'USD 42000 year' on university_scholarships row 605 was corrected in this pass. Source 2686 repointed from the bare domain to the IRS page.$note$,
  university_id = 169,
  award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'AUD', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'variable'
WHERE id = 373;

